### Session 2026-08-18 (part 2) -- M10 Method B (interpreter backend) + goal completion
- The Big Goal from M9-M10-plan.md was restarted (the previous tracker state was lost
  when the goal tools were removed mid-session; the plan file's [x] markers carried
  the completed work) and finished: 42/42 tasks.
- x86.py gained indirect call/jmp (FF /2, FF /5), accumulator-immediate arithmetic
  (05/2D/25/0D/35/3D), SIB addressing ([esp+disp] etc.), and a shim mechanism:
  registered Python callables invoked on calls to reserved guest addresses,
  with stdcall arg/clean conventions and a seeded end-marker so a bare top-level
  ret halts while nested callee rets return to the caller.
- peexec.py: Method B PE runner -- peinfo parses, sections map into the interpreter's
  flat guest memory at ImageBase+RVA, imports resolve to Win32 Python shims
  (GetStdHandle/WriteFile/ExitProcess) or loaded-DLL export addresses; guest code
  executes in the interpreter.
  - peexec-test.py 3/3: a hand-assembled PE32 with 3 kernel32 imports prints
    'Hello, Ripos!' via the WriteFile shim and exits 42.
  - peexec-dll-test.py 4/4: load_dll maps a PE32 DLL, the EXE imports mydll!my_add,
    and the interpreter RUNS the DLL's own code (mov eax,[esp+4]; add eax,[esp+8];
    ret 8) -> my_add(3,4)=7; my_greet returns a pointer to 'greetings'.
  - x86-test.py 13/13 still green after the ret-semantics change.
- Task 41: test PEs embedded (initramfs_extra/bin: mingw hello.exe + mydll.dll),
  kernel rebuilt, verified in the initramfs tar.
- Deferred with documented reasons (offline toolchain / kernel-loop constraints):
  mp3 (minimp3 not available offline), audio + waveform viz, the e1000 NIC +
  smoltcp + sockets + browser + slirp demo, and the Method A native loader
  (win64 trampolines, guest-space mapping, C shims, CRT hello).
